# LCPC-2026-07-11 — MUTATION FIXTURE. This file is deliberately wrong.
#
# Sprint 5.32's acceptance criterion is that
# `prodbox test integration control-plane-counterexample` exits 0 against the
# canonical dispositions beside this file and NON-ZERO against these. A
# reproducer that passes both is not a reproducer.
#
# The mutation: `GatewayDeadlineUnderThrottle` records the superseded
# implementation as having CLOSED the mechanism rather than having failed on it
# — i.e. it claims there was no counterexample to reproduce. Every other row is
# byte-identical to the canonical file, so the exercise isolates the disposition
# that `simulateFrozenCounterexample` must consume. Before Sprint 5.32 that
# function discarded its trace entirely, so this file and the canonical one
# produced identical output and identical exit codes.
#
# It is loaded only through `MutatedFrozenTrace`, which the validation selects
# from `PRODBOX_TEST_FROZEN_COUNTEREXAMPLE_FIXTURE=mutated`. That fixture is
# deliberately not trace-digest-pinned: pinning it would make the digest gate
# fire first and the disposition consumption — the thing under test — would
# never run. Every other captured digest is still checked, so the two fixtures
# differ in exactly one disposition and nothing else.

AbsentGetAuthorityCasMismatch           superseded-failure-observed    replacement-mechanism-closed
GatewayDeadlineUnderThrottle            replacement-mechanism-closed   replacement-mechanism-closed
SelectedTargetAuthorityEndpointMismatch superseded-failure-observed    replacement-mechanism-closed
AppliedButResponseLostRetainedOperation superseded-failure-observed    replacement-mechanism-closed
FailedSiblingSkipsIndependentRestore    superseded-failure-observed    replacement-mechanism-closed
